{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "lanes_pointwise",
    "description": "A pointwise two-species chemistry-like operator on a 6 x 5 x 4 grid. Every index-derived read a lane must compute from its cell index is here: a coordinate (cosz, a state-free observed of lat and lon computed from i and j), a level gate (an emission only where k < 2), and an affine read of an array parameter on another grid (Tsrc[k + 2], a 7-level source profile). No read leaves the cell, so the operator's locality is pointwise.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST test suite"
    ],
    "created": "2026-10-24T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "range_restricted_rhs"
    ]
  },
